:: Events Shades Remove
<<set $outside to 1>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
You reach up and take the $worn.face.name off yourself before <<he>> can.
<br><br>
River stops short, hand half-raised, and lowers it. "...Thank you."
<<He>> sounds almost disappointed to have nothing to confiscate. "See that they stay off."
<br><br>
The watching students lose interest and drift away, disappointed there was nothing to watch.
<br><br>
<<if !$settings.blindStatsEnabled>>
	<span class="blue">You put your $worn.face.name away yourself.</span>
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<status -3>><<npcincr River dom 1>><<npcincr River love 1>><<lcool>>
<<generalUndress "wardrobe" "face">>
<<courtyard>>

:: Events Shades Excuse
<<set $outside to 1>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<shadesExcuseDifficulty 600>>
<<shadesExcuseLine>>
<br><br>
<<shadesExcuseCheck>>
<br><br>
<<if $skulduggerysuccess is 1>>
	River studies you for a long moment. "...Is that documented with the infirmary?"
	<br><br>
	You hold <<his>> gaze. Eventually <<he>> exhales through <<his>> nose. "Then see that it is.
	I don't want to have this conversation twice." <<He>> marches away,
	and the watching students look faintly impressed that you got away with it.
	<br><br>
	<span class="green">You keep your $worn.face.name.</span><<status 2>><<gcool>>
<<else>>
	River doesn't even blink. "Sensitive eyes," <<he>> repeats. "How convenient."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> holds out <<his>> hand and waits, and the waiting is worse than shouting.
	<span class="red">You hand them over.</span>
	<br><br>
	"Lying to a member of staff. I'll see you in detention." <<He>> marches away with your $worn.face.name.
	<br><br>
	<<generatey2>>A <<person2>><<person>> winces on your behalf.
	<<status -10>><<gtrauma>><<trauma 6>><<detention 3>><<llcool>><<gdelinquency>>
	<<generalUndress "wardrobe" "face">>
<</if>>
<<courtyard>>


:: Sydney Chat Shades Remove
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<run statusCheck("Sydney")>>
You take the $worn.face.name off without being asked twice.
<br><br>
Sydney brightens, visibly relieved not to have had to push.
"Thank you. I know it's a silly rule, but it isn't mine to bend."
<<npcincr Sydney love 1>><<npcincr Sydney purity 1>><<glove>><<gspurity>>
<<generalUndress "wardrobe" "face">>
<br><br>
<<sydneyOptions>>


:: Sydney Chat Shades Excuse
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<run statusCheck("Sydney")>>
<<shadesExcuseDifficulty 400>>
<<shadesExcuseLine>>
<br><br>
<<shadesExcuseCheck>>
<br><br>
<<if $skulduggerysuccess is 1>>
	"Oh." Sydney's face falls immediately. "Oh, I'm sorry, I didn't... that's completely different, then."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> fidgets with <<his>> own <<sydneyGlasses>>, embarrassed.
	"I shouldn't have assumed. I'll say something if anyone else brings it up."
	<br><br>
	<span class="green">You keep your $worn.face.name,</span> and feel slightly bad about it.<<status 2>><<gcool>>
<<else>>
	Sydney looks at you for a moment too long.
	<br><br>
	"You don't wear them anywhere else," <<he>> says quietly. "Not on the way to school and at the shops."
	<<He>> doesn't sound angry, which is somehow worse. "Please just take them off."
	<br><br>
	<span class="red">You take them off.</span><<gstress>><<stress 6>><<npcincr Sydney love -2>><<llove>>
	<<generalUndress "wardrobe" "face">>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<sydneyOptions>>

:: School Changing Room Cameras
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "pool">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<set $weekly.lockerCamerasSabotaged to true>>
You return to the places where the photographs must have been taken: the vent above the showers, the clock on the wall,
and the smoke detector above the benches. You check each one carefully,
looking for anything that could hide a small camera.
<br><br>
<<if $skulduggerysuccess is 1>>
	Behind each cover, you find a small lens with wires leading into the wall.
	You open them one by one, pull the wires free from each camera, then put the covers back into place.
	<br><br>
	From the changing room, they look the same as they did before.
	<span class="green">None of the cameras can record anything now.</span>
	<br><br>
	Leighton will probably notice eventually and replace them within a week.<<llstress>><<stress -6>>
	<<if $leightonCameraSuspicion isnot "exposed">><<set $leightonCameraSuspicion to "clean">><</if>>
<<else>>
	You find the cameras hidden in the vent and smoke detector first, then remove their wires.
	The last one takes longer to find. After checking around the clock,
	you discover another small camera hidden behind it.
	<br><br>
	As you reach towards it, a red light appears beside the lens.
	You realise the camera has already started recording you. <span class="red">It saw you trying to remove it.</span>
	<br><br>
	You pull its wires free anyway and put the clock back, but whoever checks the recording may already know what you did.
	<<ggstress>><<stress 7>>
	<<set $leightonCameraSuspicion to "exposed">>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<skulduggeryuse 500>>
<<destination_pool>>

:: Shades Excuse Widgets [widget]
/*
	Pure calculation. <<shadesExcuseCheck>> updates the counter.
	Recheck before the roll because $skulduggerydifficulty can be outdated.
*/
<<widget "shadesExcuseDifficulty">>
	<<set _base to (_args[0] ?? 500)>>
	<<set _englishHelp to Math.floor(($english ?? 0) / 5)>>
	<<set _excuseUses to ($daily.shadesExcuseUses ?? 0)>>
	<<set $skulduggerydifficulty to Math.clamp(_base - _englishHelp + (_excuseUses * 150), 100, 1000)>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "shadesExcuseCheck">>
	<<set $daily.shadesExcuseUses to ($daily.shadesExcuseUses ?? 0) + 1>>
	<<skulduggerycheck>>
	<<if $skulduggerysuccess is 1>>
		<<skulduggery 3>>
	<<else>>
		<<skulduggery 1>>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

/* The excuse itself, phrased to attitude. Shared by both call-out sites. */
<<widget "shadesExcuseLine">>
	<<speechresolve>>
	<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
		<<case "meek" "shy">>
			"M-My eyes are sensitive," you say, not quite looking at <<him>>. "The light hurts."
		<<case "polite" "docile">>
			"I'm sorry," you say. "My eyes are sensitive to light. I'd rather keep them on, if that's alright."
		<<case "flamboyant">>
			"Delicate eyes, darling," you say, touching the frames. "The strip lighting in here is an assault."
		<<case "bratty" "cruel">>
			"They're for my eyes," you say flatly. "Which are sensitive. Unless you'd like to explain that to a doctor."
		<<case "confident">>
			"Sensitive eyes," you say. "Bright light gives me headaches. That's the whole story."
		<<default>>
			"My eyes are sensitive to light," you say. "That's all it is."
	<</switch>>
<</widget>>